Define the level after time \(t\) by \[L(t)=L_0+\sum_{i:t_i\le t}p_i d_i.\] The reservoir constraint requires \(L_{
min}\le L(t)\le L_{
max}\) for every \(t\). Because the level changes only at event times, it suffices to enforce these inequalities immediately after each distinct value among \(t_1,
\ldots,t_n\). Events sharing a time are aggregated in the same sum, so their internal ordering is irrelevant. Positive \(d_i\) fills the reservoir, negative \(d_i\) drains it, and \(p_i=0\) suppresses the event.

